<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 3.4 pct in September - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 3.4 pct in September - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	  SEPT 96     AUG 96   (SEPT 95)</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.3	  0.1	(0.3)</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     3.4	  3.4	(5.8)</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    104.4	104.1    (115.2)</p>
<p>Note: The 1996 data is based on a new basket of goods. The 1995 data was collated under an old basket.</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 3.5 percent for September.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     105.1	    +0.2	   +4.1</p>
<p> Clothing			 104.4	    +0.1	   +4.1</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   104.5	    +0.4	   +3.9</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 104.1	     0.0	   +3.1</p>
<p> Health spending		102.4	    -0.1	   +1.9</p>
<p> Transport			105.4	    +0.2	   +3.9</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.6	    +1.1	   +2.8</p>
<p> Education			104.7	    +0.6	   +2.9</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  104.6	    +0.1	   +3.7</p>
<p> Other goods,service	  103.1	     0.0	   +1.9</p>
<p>(including communications)  </p>
<p>Note: - Istat said in the first nine months of the year inflation rose 4.2 percent against the same period in 1995. The government has said average annual inflation in 1996 will be 3.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
